  "source": "binary-search.glon",
  "domain": "A block of integers sorted ascending; the algorithm does not sort or validate ordering.",
  "description": "Return the zero-based index of a target integer in an ascending block, or -1 when absent. For duplicates any matching index is acceptable. The implementation is the proposed recursive binary search; input blocks are read-only.",
  "attribution": "Problem definition: Rosetta Code, 'Binary search' (https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Binary_search). The Glon implementation is the proposed version. The referenced Rosetta Code page currently publishes no REBOL solution, so no REBOL listing is invented or included.",
  "reference": "Expected indices are generated independently with Python bisect_left for sorted unique blocks. Duplicate cases use the acceptance helper binary-search-found and require the returned index to hold the target value, not a particular duplicate index. Input preservation is checked separately.",
  "family_note": "Rosetta Code challenge; separate from REBOL Cookbook challenges.",
